course: dictionary
lesson: 5932
title: Marvel and marvelling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A marvel is a wonderful, amazing thing or person. To marvel at something means to feel great surprise and admiration, so you stop, stare and think, wow. The word works as a noun (a marvel) and as a verb (to marvel).
explain: Look at the words around it. «The marvels of nature» are amazing things in nature, and «the marvels of technology» are amazing machines and inventions. The little word at tells you what you are admiring: people marvel at the stars.
explain: Watch for capital letters. In «Marvel's Thor», the capital M and the 's show a name, not the ordinary word marvel. Swap in your meaning to check: a wonder's Thor does not make sense, so the sentence is talking about a name.
fact: A marvel is a wonderful, amazing thing or person.
fact: To marvel at something means to feel great surprise and admiration.
fact: «Valhalla» was the hall of fallen warriors in the Viking myths.
fact: Marvel can be a noun (a marvel, marvels) or a verb (marvel, marvelled or marveled, marvelling or marveling).
fact: A capital letter, as in «Marvel's Thor», often means a name, not the ordinary word.
exercise: «It's a marvel you didn't fall.» Here, marvel means | *Something amazing, a true wonder | A loud noise | A small, sad cloud | Something amazing or lucky to see
exercise: Sam stood under the stars and began to marvel. What does marvel mean here? | To shout at the sky | To fall asleep | To count the stars quickly | *To feel great surprise and admiration
exercise: «The marvels of technology» are amazing inventions. Which word in that phrase names the amazing things? | the | *marvels | of | technology
test: Why might a child marvel at a rainbow? | Because it is very small | Because rainbows cost money | Because it is a grey, wet day | *Because it is a wonder of nature and looks amazing
test: Which sentence uses marvel as a name, not the ordinary word? | «It was a marvel of engineering.» | «We marveled at the stars.» | *«Marvel's Thor is very different from the old myths.» | «The marvel of the year was the rainbow.»
exam: What does the phrase «a marvel of» show? | Something very small | A sort of puzzle | *Something wonderful, like «a marvel of engineering» | An old word for a castle
